B.aG6=new A.kq("Liber et Libri is a free library of classic books with a focus (speed-reading) mode. Everything you read is stored only on this device. There are no accounts and no tracking.",null)
B.aG7=new A.kq("Speed-read mode shows one word at a time. It is great for focus and for getting through a chapter, but research shows that reading much faster usually costs some comprehension. Pick a pace that feels comfortable and switch back to the page whenever you like.",null)
B.aG8=new A.kq("Pride and Prejudice: plates by Hugh Thomson (George Allen, 1894) and C. E. Brock (Macmillan, 1895). Frankenstein: frontispiece and title-page vignette by Theodor von Holst, engraved by W. Chevalier (Colburn & Bentley, 1831). All are public domain; scans from Wikimedia Commons. Full per-plate sources are listed in the app\u2019s attribution file.",null)
B.aG9=new A.kq("Definitions come from Webster\u2019s Revised Unabridged Dictionary (G. & C. Merriam Co., 1913), a public-domain work, via the Project Gutenberg text (gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765) as parsed by the WebstersEnglishDictionary project on GitHub. Definitions are shortened to their first senses; being from 1913, they reflect the usage and attitudes of their time.",null)
B.aGa=new A.kq("All books come from Standard Ebooks (standardebooks.org), a volunteer project that produces carefully proofread, beautifully formatted editions of public-domain works.",null)
B.aGb=new A.kq("Recordings are LibriVox (librivox.org) public-domain audiobooks read by volunteers, streamed from the Internet Archive (archive.org); each player names its reader. Read-along timing for a few pilot chapters was produced on our side by automatically aligning the recording with the text, so it can drift by a word or two. Liber et Libri is not affiliated with LibriVox or the Internet Archive.",null)
B.aGc=new A.kq("For reading in the app, the text has been converted to plain paragraphs; endnotes and some typographic details were left out.",null)
B.aGd=new A.kq("Standard Ebooks dedicates its editions (their formatting, proofreading and cover designs) to the public domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication (creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). The underlying texts are believed to be in the public domain in the United States; copyright status may differ in other countries. Liber et Libri is not affiliated with or endorsed by Standard Ebooks.",null)
